Subject: [PATCH] Re-add deleted_at to nested resource schemas

Speakeasy's soft-delete handling strips deleted_at from schemas that nest an
entity-root struct while retaining the field in the generated Go model. The
framework then rejects plans and applies because the struct and object shape
differ. Restore deleted_at in all seven protected nested schemas.

diff --git a/internal/provider/app_entitlement_owner_entitlement_resource.go b/internal/provider/app_entitlement_owner_entitlement_resource.go
index 6ae2bc1a..ee15287e 100644
--- a/internal/provider/app_entitlement_owner_entitlement_resource.go
+++ b/internal/provider/app_entitlement_owner_entitlement_resource.go
@@ -108,6 +108,9 @@ func (r *AppEntitlementOwnerEntitlementResource) Schema(ctx context.Context, req
 						Computed:    true,
 						Description: `Flag to indicate if app-level access request defaults have been applied to the entitlement`,
 					},
+					"deleted_at": schema.StringAttribute{
+						Computed: true,
+					},
 					"deprovisioner_policy": schema.SingleNestedAttribute{
 						Computed: true,
 						Attributes: map[string]schema.Attribute{
